      "id": "bug",
      "text": "Most devs blame the query here."
    },
    {
      "id": "why",
      "text": "The culprit can be bpchar with no length. B-tree deduplication could make index-only scans wrong."
    },
    {
      "id": "fix",
      "text": "November's update turns it off. Update, then REINDEX. Char with a length is safe. New columns? Use VARCHAR or TEXT."
    },
